# ============================================================
# .gitignore — 578-EHRM-TrainingSchedulerApp
# Last updated: 2026-09-11
#
# This repository is PUBLIC-mirrored, so the default stance is to
# ignore anything that is local-only, machine-generated, a binary
# or data export, or potentially sensitive (PII / secrets / VA
# internal data). Public-facing source lives under src/, docs/,
# assets/, .github/ and .vscode/ and is tracked normally.
#
# To force-track a file that a rule below ignores: add a negation
# ( ! ) AFTER the rule that ignores it, then run `git add -f <file>`.
# A negation cannot re-include a file when a PARENT DIRECTORY is
# ignored — un-ignore the directory first, then the file.
# ============================================================


# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Temporary / build / export output (regenerated, local-only)
#    dist/ = pac canvas/solution exports; tmp/ = scratch space.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
/temp/
/.temp/
/dist/

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Local-only retention & config (never mirrored)
#    archive/ = pre-change snapshots mirroring the src/ layout.
#    config/  = runbooks / env templates / tooling helpers
#               (recreated on demand by the solution-unpack task).
# ------------------------------------------------------------
/archive/
/config/
/optionalGUI/

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Local-only working folders (matched by NAME at any depth)
#    Any folder literally named `local` or `.local` is scratch
#    space and is never committed — e.g. docs/local/, assets/local/,
#    src/analytics/{sql,powerBI}/local/, src/sharePoint/list/*/local/
#    (raw list exports). This single rule supersedes the old
#    per-path entries (docs/local/, src/config/local/, etc.).
# ------------------------------------------------------------
local/
.local/
/docs/logs/
/docs/release-notes/releaseTemplates/

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Secrets & environment-specific values
# ------------------------------------------------------------
*.env
*.env.*
.secrets/
secrets.*
credentials.*

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. OS / editor generated files
#    NOTE: .vscode/ is intentionally TRACKED (shared workspace,
#    tasks, settings, extensions) — do NOT ignore it. .vs/ is
#    Visual Studio's local cache and IS ignored.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Dependencies, caches & language build artifacts
#    Python venvs MUST live on local disk, never in-repo: a venv
#    on this S:\ SMB share breaks Jupyter/Data Wrangler kernels.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
coverage/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Backup, log & swap files
#    (Exported *.log files can contain MSAL auth tokens — the
#    extension rule keeps them out of the mirror.)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Binary packages & compressed archives
#    Large/binary exports are blocked by default. The deliberate
#    EXCEPTIONS that stay tracked are Canvas .msapp packages and
#    Power BI .pbit templates; each negation must follow the rule
#    it overrides. src/**/.zip/** ignores everything inside any
#    `.zip` export folder under src/.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Canvas app packages & solution exports
*.zip
!*.msapp
src/**/.zip/**

# Compressed archive formats
*.7z
*.gz
*.bz2
*.tar
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.tar.bz2
*.rar

# Power BI (ignore large binary .pbix; keep .pbit templates)
*.pbix
!*.pbit

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Data / spreadsheet files (PII & VA-internal data guard)
#    Ignored by extension anywhere in the tree, so raw exports
#    cannot be committed by accident. To publish one sanitized
#    file, negate it below and run `git add -f`, e.g.:
#      !src/sharePoint/list/desks/local/Desks.csv
# ------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.xlsb
*.ods

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Raw TMS extracts — deny-all, publish only docs & shortcuts
#     src/analytics/tms/ holds raw TMS data exports (PII), so the
#     entire subtree is ignored by default. The only PUBLISHED
#     files are the component README and the Power BI / SharePoint
#     .url shortcuts. The parent dir is re-included first because
#     Git cannot re-include a file beneath an excluded directory.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
/src/analytics/tms/**
!/src/analytics/tms/README.md
!/src/analytics/tms/lists/*.url
